WEBVTT

02:07.081 --> 02:10.126 align:center line:79%
Eventually, God spoke
to Job from a whirlwind.

02:10.668 --> 02:14.088 align:center line:79%
God didn’t defend himself
or explain Job’s suffering.

02:14.088 --> 02:14.755 align:center line:81%
[Music]

02:14.755 --> 02:18.509 align:center line:79%
Rather, God highlighted the ignorance
of Job and his friends

02:18.509 --> 02:21.429 align:center line:81%
and posed at least 66 questions.

02:22.096 --> 02:24.015 align:center line:81%
Job couldn't answer even one.

02:24.015 --> 02:24.765 align:center line:81%
[Music]

02:24.765 --> 02:27.685 align:center line:79%
It was as if God
had patiently said to Job,

02:28.352 --> 02:32.106 align:center line:79%
If you can’t answer
any of my questions about this world,

02:32.732 --> 02:36.569 align:center line:79%
is it possible that eternal laws
exist that you don't understand?

02:37.320 --> 02:40.239 align:center line:79%
Are there assumptions
you've made that are invalid?

02:40.865 --> 02:44.619 align:center line:79%
And can you foresee
your intended future destiny?

02:44.619 --> 02:45.953 align:center line:81%
[Music]

02:45.953 --> 02:48.873 align:center line:81%
Job grasped God's message.

02:49.457 --> 02:52.668 align:center line:79%
He humbly acknowledged
that he hadn't understood.

02:52.668 --> 02:56.380 align:center line:79%
He recognized that though
all sin causes suffering,

02:57.048 --> 02:59.717 align:center line:81%
not all suffering is caused by sin.

03:00.301 --> 03:03.554 align:center line:79%
Because his suffering wasn’t
caused by sin,

03:03.971 --> 03:06.766 align:center line:81%
Job’s job was to trust God.

03:07.600 --> 03:09.518 align:center line:81%
Because of his trust in God,

03:09.518 --> 03:15.024 align:center line:79%
Job learned that “when [God] hath
tried me, I shall come forth as gold,”

03:15.691 --> 03:19.654 align:center line:79%
and “though he slay me,
yet will I trust . . . him.”

03:19.654 --> 03:20.738 align:center line:81%
[Music]

03:20.738 --> 03:25.159 align:center line:79%
Like Job, we need to trust
in our Heavenly Father in Jesus Christ

03:25.368 --> 03:28.371 align:center line:81%
and remain faithful in all circumstances.

03:28.371 --> 03:29.455 align:center line:81%
[Music]

03:29.455 --> 03:33.793 align:center line:79%
Job's testimony of the Savior
is inspiring thousands of years

03:33.793 --> 03:37.588 align:center line:79%
after he uttered it.
And it's my testimony as well.

03:37.588 --> 03:38.839 align:center line:81%
[Music]

03:38.839 --> 03:40.883 align:center line:81%
“Oh that my words were now written!

03:41.634 --> 03:44.220 align:center line:81%
oh that they were printed in a book!

03:44.220 --> 03:49.350 align:center line:79%
That they were graven with an iron
pen and lead in the rock for ever!

03:50.101 --> 03:52.561 align:center line:81%
For I know that my redeemer liveth,

03:52.937 --> 03:56.315 align:center line:79%
and that he shall stand
at the latter day upon the earth:

03:57.692 --> 04:03.281 align:center line:79%
And though . . . worms destroy this body,
yet in my flesh shall I see God.”

04:03.281 --> 04:04.365 align:center line:81%
[Music]

04:04.365 --> 04:08.411 align:center line:79%
Jesus Christ won't just
console us and restore what was lost,

04:09.078 --> 04:12.832 align:center line:79%
but He will even consecrate
our afflictions for our gain.

04:12.832 --> 04:14.083 align:center line:81%
[Music]

04:14.083 --> 04:18.963 align:center line:79%
The Savior has the power to make
everything right, and He yearns to do so.

04:18.963 --> 04:19.755 align:center line:81%
[Music]

04:19.755 --> 04:25.011 align:center line:79%
The ultimate lesson of the book
of Job is that our job, like Job’s,

04:25.052 --> 04:27.555 align:center line:81%
is to trust God—no matter what.

04:28.264 --> 04:34.437 align:center line:79%
These teachings encourage us to let
God prevail so that we remain optimistic

04:34.437 --> 04:36.939 align:center line:81%
and hopeful despite challenges.

04:37.523 --> 04:40.234 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ, amen.
